invariant: INV-10
file: tls_write.c
catches: tcp_blocking_key_limit
reason: the ceiling is counted one record too late, so ch_write seals a data
  record at the key's last sequence number and puts the KeyUpdate at
  REC_AES_GCM_RECORDS_MAX, a record past what the key may seal, where
  rec_seal refuses it. The boundary case expects the KeyUpdate before the
  second record.

--- old
    uint64_t last = REC_AES_GCM_RECORDS_MAX - 1;
--- new
    uint64_t last = REC_AES_GCM_RECORDS_MAX;
